\title{Value}
\date{2026-11-11T11:48:36Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}
\import{flow-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{The \em{value} of a [flow](00RZ) #{f} is defined as the amount of flow leaving the source: ##{v(f) = \fout(s).}}

\p{Note that because the total flow must be preserved at each vertex, it should be intuitively clear that ##{\fout(s) = \fin(t)} so we could equally well define the value of a flow #{v(f)} as the amount of flow arriving at the target. In fact, proving this formally is a good exercise.}
